   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Before the verb or attached to it",
     "texto": [
      "With a conjugated verb, the pronoun goes **before**: **lo** compro. In a negative command too: **no me llames**.\n\nWith a verb followed by an **infinitive** or **gerund**, there are two places:\n\n- **Lo** quiero ver = quiero ver**lo**.\n- **Lo** estoy haciendo = estoy haciéndo**lo**.\n\nIt never goes in the middle: you do not say «quiero lo ver».\n\nWith an **affirmative command**, the pronoun sticks to the end: di**me**, llá**ma**me, dá**me**lo, siénta**te**. You often need an **accent** so the stress does not move."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Two places for the pronoun",
     "texto": [
      "Compare the two positions:\n\n- **Lo** quiero ver. = Quiero ver**lo**.\n- **Te** voy a llamar. = Voy a llamar**te**.\n- **Lo** estoy haciendo. = Estoy haciéndo**lo**.\n- With a command: llámame, dámelo (only attached).\n- With «no»: **no me** llames (only before).\n\nIf you attach two pronouns, they keep the usual order: first who receives, then the thing: dá**melo**, pá**samela**."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
